+# EduPulse â€” Ù…Ø³Ø§Ø­Ø© Ø¹Ù…Ù„ Ø§Ù„Ù…Ø¤Ø³Ø³Ø© Ø§Ù„ØªØ¹Ù„ÙŠÙ…ÙŠØ©
 
+EduPulse is an Arabic-first (RTL) institution platform for an Algerian school: a staff workspace over
+learners, records, attendance, payments with printable/PDF receipts, LMD supervision, and AI teaching
+tools â€” plus a learner portal with notes, quizzes and spaced repetition. Every control in the
+interior is wired to a real tRPC procedure that reads and writes data; nothing in the workspace is a
+decorative button.
+
+Dark canvas, Instrument Serif display type, thin liquid-glass panels, `ws-*` workspace design layer
+(`client/src/index.css`). Arabic is the default language everywhere, including receipts, printed
+reports and research output.
+
+## Open it in 10 seconds
+
+```bash
+corepack pnpm install
+corepack pnpm run dev:demo     # guest mode: an in-memory institution, no database needed
+```
+
+Then load `http://localhost:3000/`. **The root URL opens straight into the workspace** â€” the rail on
+the right, the briefing overview, and the demo staff identity signed in â€” because in demo/guest mode
+the interior _is_ the product and is not hidden behind the marketing hero.
+
+| URL               | What you land on                                                                |
+| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `/`               | Staff workspace: overview, learners, records, receipts, LMD supervision         |
+| `/?as=learner`    | Learner portal: today's due cards, quiz, progress (demo learner signed in)      |
+| `/?open=research` | Research studio â€” BM25 over the approved corpus, cited `[S#]` report            |
+| `/?open=payments` | Payments & receipts: record a payment, print or download the Arabic receipt PDF |
+| `/hero`           | The public marketing front door (hero preserved exactly as supplied)            |
+
+Signed out on a real deployment? You get the sign-in panel over the same cinematic backdrop â€” still no
+landing page to scroll. The front door stays at `/hero`.
+
+`?open=<view>` accepts any rail view id. Views are role-gated: opening one the current identity may
+not read shows a refusal toast instead of a broken panel.
+
+Persistence note: `dev:demo` keeps the institution in memory (no DB reachable is the normal case in
+a sandbox), so a server restart resets the demo rows. Everything else â€” the same procedures, the same
+role checks, the same return shapes â€” runs unchanged; `docs/portable-deployment.md` covers the real
+MySQL/TiDB deployment where the writes are durable.
+
+## Where things are
+
+| Path                                                                    | Contents                                                                                    |
+| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `client/src/components/EduPulseApp.tsx`                                 | App shell: entry decision, roles, navigation, views, receipts                               |
+| `client/src/components/entryScreen.ts`                                  | Pure rule for what opens at `/` (guarded by `entryScreen.test.ts`)                          |
+| `client/src/components/WorkspaceOverview.tsx`, `WorkspaceDirectory.tsx` | Rebuilt interior dashboard and learner directory                                            |
+| `client/src/components/StudentQuizPanel.tsx`, `creator/*`               | Quiz loop, research studio, AI console, creator studio                                      |
+| `server/guestStore.ts`                                                  | The in-memory institution behind guest mode                                                 |
+| `server/creator/{quizEngine,research,adaptive}.ts`                      | Grading/FSRS/BM25 engines, with hermetic tests                                              |
+| `drizzle/`                                                              | SQL migrations (`0013_quiz_attempts.sql` is the newest interior addition)                   |
+| `screenshots/`                                                          | Rendered evidence of the quiz loop and the research studio                                  |
+| `session-patches/`                                                      | Re-applicable diff of the interior rebuild for a clean checkout                             |
+| `docs/`                                                                 | Portable deployment, integration design, handoff notes                                      |
+| `docs/SHIP-TO-MAIN.md`                                                  | How to get this onto `main` so the deployed web interface changes (the sandbox cannot push) |
+
+## Quality gates
+
+```bash
+corepack pnpm run check    # tsc --noEmit â€” must be silent
+corepack pnpm test         # vitest, hermetic, no network
+corepack pnpm run build    # Vite client + esbuild server bundle
+```
 
 ## GitHub Pages static preview
 
 The repository includes `.github/workflows/pages.yml`, which publishes the Vite frontend to GitHub Pages on pushes to `main`. After the first successful workflow, enable **Settings â†’ Pages â†’ GitHub Actions** if GitHub has not enabled it automatically. The default URL is `https://NourTi.github.io/edupulse/`; a custom domain can be configured in the Pages settings after you own and verify that domain.
 
-GitHub Pages serves only the static frontend. EduPulse password authentication, institution memberships, MySQL records, Resend recovery, storage, and the grounded RAG procedures require the full server deployment and remain intended for Manus WebDev or another Node-capable host. The Pages build is therefore a public product/landing preview, not a substitute for the production backend.
-
+GitHub Pages serves only the static frontend. EduPulse password sessions, institution memberships, MySQL records, Resend recovery, storage, and the grounded RAG procedures require the full server deployment and remain intended for Manus WebDev or another Node-capable host. The Pages build is therefore a public product/landing preview, not a substitute for the production backend.
 
 For running the complete application outside Manus, see [`docs/portable-deployment.md`](docs/portable-deployment.md). It defines the Node 22 build/start contract, database and secret variables, Resend requirements, portable storage/LLM boundaries, and the distinction between GitHub Pages and full-stack hosting.
