+## 7. Environment traps (each one already cost a debugging cycle)
+
+1. **The sandbox can be recreated at any time.** Only `/home/user/edupulse` is restored â€” and even that is
+   rewound to the merge base, with `node_modules` and the running dev server deleted. Three recreations have
+   happened in this session; each time `git log` looked empty while the working tree still held every file, and
+   each time the work was recovered by re-committing (`git status --short | wc -l`, grep for content markers,
+   then `git add -A && git commit`). Check that before rebuilding anything, and treat the committed
+   `session-patches/` diff as the durable artifact because local commit objects do not survive.
+2. `git commit -m` containing backticks is destructive in this shell. Use `git commit -F /tmp/msg.txt`.
+3. `pkill -f "pattern"` inside a compound command can kill the shell running it. Kill by explicit PID.
+4. Vitest can steal the dev port; stop the dev server before `pnpm test`, and expect a fallback port
+   (`Port 3000 is busy, using 3001`) which silently breaks the live preview.
+5. Sandbox egress is npm-registry-only: no apt/Debian mirror, no `storage.googleapis.com`, no CDN fonts.
+   Headless Chromium here needs `libnss3`, which is missing â†’ **screenshots may be impossible in a fresh
+   sandbox**. Fonts must be bundled (`@fontsource/*`), never CDN-loaded.
+6. Arabic in an HTTP header value throws before send â†’ percent-encode.
+7. Inside RTL, Latin fragments need `dir="auto"`.
+8. Probes must be written at the project root and run with `npx tsx` (not from `/tmp`).
+9. `grep -c "export function X" file` returning 0 does not mean the feature is gone â€” grep the bare name.
+10. **Never build the hand-off patch from the working tree.** A plain `git diff <commit>` ignores untracked
+    files, so a patch generated that way silently drops every new file â€” it happened here: `guestStore.ts`,
+    `knowledge/freeData.ts`, `aiConsole.ts` and `entryScreen.ts` vanished, and the receiving checkout failed
+    `tsc` with "Cannot find module" while only 46 of 160 test files existed. Always `git add -A` and commit
+    first, then `git diff <main>..<HEAD>`, and verify by applying the patch on a clean worktree of `main` and
+    running tsc + vitest + build there.
+11. Deliverables in `session-patches/` are large by design (1.3â€“2.8 MB each); don't "clean" them, and don't
+    add new huge artifacts outside the repo's ignore conventions.
